    "text": "Perfect! The refactoring is complete and all 29 tests pass. Here's a summary of the improvements:\n\n## Refactoring Summary\n\n### **IFs and Duplicated Code Removed:**\n\n1. **Eliminated nested IFs in `CustomerImporter>>importCustomer`**\n   - Old: Multiple nested IFs checking `idType = 'D'` vs `idType = 'C'` with validation logic scattered\n   - New: Delegates to `IdentificationType` polymorphic hierarchy\n\n2. **Eliminated nested IFs in `CustomerImporter>>importAddress`**\n   - Old: Multiple nested IFs checking if zipcode is numeric or letter-based\n   - New: Delegates to `ZipCode` polymorphic hierarchy\n\n### **Polymorphic Design Introduced:**\n\n**IdentificationType Hierarchy:**\n- `IdentificationType` (abstract) with factory method `from:number:`\n- `DNIIdentification` - encapsulates DNI validation (all digits, 1-99999999)\n- `CUITIdentification` - encapsulates CUIT validation (format with dashes, header checks, etc.)\n\n**ZipCode Hierarchy:**\n- `ZipCode` (abstract) with factory method `from:`\n- `OldZipCode` - encapsulates old format validation (numeric 1000-9999)\n- `NewZipCode` - encapsulates new format validation (letter + 4 digits + 3 letters)\n\n### **Benefits:**\n- \u2705 All complex validation logic moved to type-specific classes\n- \u2705 CustomerImporter is now declarative and easy to read\n- \u2705 Easy to extend: adding new identification/zipcode types requires only new subclasses\n- \u2705 No code duplication\n- \u2705 All 29 tests pass without modification"
